{{Short description|Football tournament details}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Play in '''Group F of the [[1990 FIFA World Cup]]''' completed on 21 June 1990. [[England national football team|England]] won the group and advanced to the second round, along with the [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]] and the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]]. [[Egypt national football team|Egypt]] failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/90full.html |title=World Cup 1990 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> This group has the record (along with the 1982 Group 1) of the most draws (five) of any "group round" in World Cup history. Both the [[Republic of Ireland]] and the [[Netherlands]] advanced but finished with identical records—with identical points, goal difference, goals scored, as well as drawing with each other—resulting in the drawing of lots to determine their position.

